WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:05.106
- I was a hometown kid.

00:01:08.651 --> 00:01:10.779
I was a Player of the Year candidate.

00:01:10.945 --> 00:01:12.363
- [Announcer]: Here comes the All-America!

00:01:13.782 --> 00:01:17.160
- The nation's leading scorer at nearly 29 points per game. 

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.746
- [Mark Few]: The bigger the moment, you know, the better he was.

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:23.291
- [Announcer]: Kid has been compared to Larry Bird.

00:01:23.666 --> 00:01:27.629
- I think I had five 40-point games that season. I was really rolling offensively.

00:01:30.006 --> 00:01:31.925
My expectation was Final Four, to be honest.

00:01:38.056 --> 00:01:41.184
- [Announcer]: Now, let's head courtside along with

00:01:41.184 --> 00:01:43.103
former Gonzaga standout Adam Morrison.

00:01:45.063 --> 00:01:46.439
- Nobody prepares you for fame.

00:01:47.816 --> 00:01:50.026
I get remembered for showing emotion.

00:01:51.903 --> 00:01:53.404
But during that season,

00:01:53.404 --> 00:01:56.032
I felt that I was one of the better players in college basketball,

00:01:56.032 --> 00:01:57.534
and I think I proved that.

00:01:57.909 --> 00:01:59.452
- [Announcer]: Here's Morrison. Book it.

00:02:00.495 --> 00:02:01.996
- There he is again!

00:02:01.996 --> 00:02:02.956
He's got 34.

00:02:04.415 --> 00:02:05.959
- I was a big Larry Bird fan

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:07.919
and I wanted to be like him in every aspect.

00:02:09.003 --> 00:02:10.421
So it kinda came and stuck.

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:14.300
- [Announcer]: He told me that he studies Larry Bird.

00:02:15.093 --> 00:02:16.678
- He obviously loved Larry Bird

00:02:16.678 --> 00:02:18.221
and looked up to Larry Bird.

00:02:18.221 --> 00:02:19.430
I mean, and, you know,

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:21.391
the elbow—pocket was way up high.

00:02:22.642 --> 00:02:23.643
- The mustache,

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:25.103
everybody remembers his.

00:02:25.103 --> 00:02:26.688
So that was part of it,

00:02:26.688 --> 00:02:28.398
and then the media took ahold of it,

00:02:28.398 --> 00:02:29.941
and it kinda just took a life upon itself.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:32.944
Looking back on it now,

00:02:32.944 --> 00:02:34.779
there's times where I'm like—

00:02:34.779 --> 00:02:36.614
But also it created a brand for myself.

00:02:37.949 --> 00:02:39.159
- Once you watch him for a while,

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:41.119
you realize it's different,

00:02:41.119 --> 00:02:42.745
and it's—and it's unorthodox

00:02:42.745 --> 00:02:44.873
but it's incredibly effective. 

00:02:44.873 --> 00:02:46.541
I mean, the way he can really,

00:02:46.541 --> 00:02:47.792
really, really score the ball.

00:02:53.381 --> 00:02:55.800
- [Announcer]: Morrison falling away from the corner!

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:57.677
- It was fun because I had the ultimate green light.

00:02:57.677 --> 00:02:59.345
I could shoot whenever I wanted.

00:02:59.888 --> 00:03:02.015
- [Announcer]: Morrison tries one from about

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:03.391
30 feet away!

00:03:03.766 --> 00:03:05.810
- Well, I was obviously a very emotional player.

00:03:08.479 --> 00:03:10.231
It created an image 

00:03:10.231 --> 00:03:11.774
and so much media attention as well.

00:03:12.233 --> 00:03:13.776
- He had a tendency to talk,

00:03:13.776 --> 00:03:15.111
and that kinda got him going.

00:03:16.738 --> 00:03:18.239
And that was just Adam

00:03:21.326 --> 00:03:22.869
That year with Adam,

00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:24.204
it was amazing.

00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:25.163
Not only were we highly ranked,

00:03:25.163 --> 00:03:30.168
but he was such an entity that everybody wanted to see.

00:03:30.168 --> 00:03:31.211
I mean,

00:03:31.211 --> 00:03:32.212
he had to check in under aliases,

00:03:32.212 --> 00:03:33.171
you know, in hotels.

00:03:33.504 --> 00:03:34.589
- Dirk Diggler.

00:03:34.589 --> 00:03:36.174
I know I used Dirk Diggler for a while

00:03:36.174 --> 00:03:39.177
which, um, hopefully my kids don't watch this.

00:03:40.136 --> 00:03:42.388
- And then we’d walk into these arenas

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:45.141
and they were raring to go hours before tip.

00:03:45.141 --> 00:03:47.602
And he would just thrive in that environment.

00:03:47.977 --> 00:03:51.272
- [Announcer]: He's like the fifth Beatle with the paparazzi following him.

00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:55.443
- [Crowd chanting]: One more year! One more year!

00:03:55.443 --> 00:03:58.154
- It was such a whirlwind around me.

00:03:58.154 --> 00:04:00.156
You know, I look at a double-edged sword.

00:04:00.156 --> 00:04:03.243
It was great, but also there was times where I was like,

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:05.703
“Can I just disappear and just be a normal college kid?”

00:04:06.454 --> 00:04:08.039
I felt a little bit bad

00:04:08.039 --> 00:04:11.501
that it took away from kind of my other teammates’ success

00:04:11.501 --> 00:04:13.378
but also it helped elevate the program and

00:04:13.378 --> 00:04:17.715
gave us an opportunity to take a step from, you know,

00:04:17.715 --> 00:04:20.301
mid-major and now to a true powerhouse.

00:04:20.843 --> 00:04:22.387
There was so much pressure

00:04:22.387 --> 00:04:25.515
because of who I was and how the season progressed.

00:04:26.808 --> 00:04:28.810
We thought we were a Final Four team.

00:04:30.645 --> 00:04:33.314
- [Announcer]: Adam Morrison, National Player of the Year candidate,

00:04:33.314 --> 00:04:36.276
trying to put Gonzaga on his back on a tournament run.

00:04:40.196 --> 00:04:41.906
- We were a three seed that year,

00:04:41.906 --> 00:04:42.907
but we liked our draw.

00:04:43.908 --> 00:04:45.410
- [Announcer]: Morrison for the lead.

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:46.327
Got it!

00:04:46.828 --> 00:04:49.080
- I hit a three late in that game down the stretch

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:50.415
to really extend ourselves.

00:04:56.754 --> 00:04:58.589
We had a tough game against Indiana

00:04:58.589 --> 00:05:01.217
and squeaked by in the second round.

00:05:03.511 --> 00:05:05.138
And then everybody knows the UCLA game.

00:05:06.681 --> 00:05:08.725
- [Announcer]: UCLA and Gonzaga 

00:05:08.725 --> 00:05:09.934
for a trip to the final eight.

00:05:10.393 --> 00:05:12.687
- Here comes the All-America.

00:05:12.687 --> 00:05:15.356
- We hadn’t been in the Sweet 16 in my two years before that.

00:05:15.356 --> 00:05:16.691
We lost in the second round.

00:05:16.691 --> 00:05:18.151
So there was a lot of pressure on us, for sure.

00:05:18.651 --> 00:05:21.112
- [Announcer]: Gonzaga by 17.

00:05:21.112 --> 00:05:23.948
Morrison, quick-release three.

00:05:23.948 --> 00:05:25.408
Pure, and the foul!

00:05:25.408 --> 00:05:27.118
- We weren’t looking ahead, but when you're up 17

00:05:27.118 --> 00:05:28.077
at one point,

00:05:28.077 --> 00:05:29.203
it’s hard not to a little bit.

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:30.621
- [Announcer]: Afflalo, block.  

00:05:30.621 --> 00:05:32.332
Gets his own rebound. 

00:05:32.332 --> 00:05:33.458
And-1!

00:05:33.875 --> 00:05:36.169
Now we've got a ballgame.

00:05:36.711 --> 00:05:38.713
- This one's not over.

00:05:38.713 --> 00:05:39.922
- Here come the Bruins!

00:05:39.922 --> 00:05:43.843
- Literally everything that had to go right for them down the stretch did.

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:46.346
Some guys hit some pretty amazing shots for them.

00:05:46.346 --> 00:05:48.389
You know, it was just, just one of those games.

00:05:48.389 --> 00:05:49.932
- [Announcer]: Farmar, runner,

00:05:49.932 --> 00:05:50.892
got it!

00:05:51.726 --> 00:05:53.644
- It just kinda happened in a fog.

00:05:53.644 --> 00:05:56.022
- [Announcer]: Morrison, step-back jumper, deep, 

00:05:56.022 --> 00:05:57.023
off the heel. 

00:05:57.023 --> 00:05:58.107
Loose ball...

00:05:58.107 --> 00:05:59.108
and a foul!

00:05:59.108 --> 00:06:00.860
It will go against Batista.

00:06:01.235 --> 00:06:02.570
- That's one of my biggest regrets.

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:03.821
I should have bounced him down and probably

00:06:03.821 --> 00:06:05.740
got closer and tried to get fouled.

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:08.534
And once I missed that, everything kinda—domino effect,

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:09.535
and then got a little bit crazy.

00:06:09.535 --> 00:06:10.536
- [Announcer]: 71-70.

00:06:12.705 --> 00:06:14.040
They throw it to Morrison. 

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:15.666
He holds on.

00:06:15.666 --> 00:06:16.959
- You don’t wanna foul Morrison.

00:06:16.959 --> 00:06:18.294
You make him get it over half court.

00:06:18.294 --> 00:06:19.253
You know you got a foul.

00:06:19.253 --> 00:06:20.254
- And a steal!

00:06:20.254 --> 00:06:21.381
Farmar, 

00:06:21.381 --> 00:06:22.548
inside 

00:06:22.715 --> 00:06:23.716
the freshman up...

00:06:23.716 --> 00:06:26.469
ohhh, and they go in front!

00:06:26.469 --> 00:06:27.470
Raivio,

00:06:27.470 --> 00:06:28.846
last chance today—

00:06:28.846 --> 00:06:30.431
oh, Mbah a Moute!

00:06:30.431 --> 00:06:31.391
- Unbelievable!

00:06:31.391 --> 00:06:32.725
- Oh, what a game!

00:06:32.725 --> 00:06:33.684
- Unbelievable!

00:06:33.684 --> 00:06:34.894
- What a game!

00:06:34.894 --> 00:06:35.895
- Unbelievable!

00:06:35.895 --> 00:06:39.148
- UCLA! Unbelievable!

00:06:39.982 --> 00:06:41.401
- Are you kidding me?!

00:06:41.401 --> 00:06:42.610
- Adam Morrison,

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:44.112
is this it for him?

00:06:44.112 --> 00:06:45.071
After leading the entire ballgame.

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:49.534
- Look up and we’re down.

00:06:49.534 --> 00:06:50.535
It was tough.

00:06:50.535 --> 00:06:52.453
It was tough to handle, to be honest.

00:06:52.829 --> 00:06:53.913
I'm sure there's time

00:06:53.913 --> 00:06:54.914
when he probably still thinks about it 

00:06:54.914 --> 00:06:55.915
to this day.

00:06:57.417 --> 00:06:58.751
- [Announcer]: The frontcourt,

00:06:58.751 --> 00:07:00.753
Batista with the catch…

00:07:01.504 --> 00:07:02.964
And that’s it!

00:07:02.964 --> 00:07:04.173
What a comeback!

00:07:04.173 --> 00:07:05.675
U-C-L-A 

00:07:06.384 --> 00:07:08.052
defeats Gonzaga, 

00:07:08.052 --> 00:07:09.971
73-71,

00:07:09.971 --> 00:07:12.598
after being down by 17!

00:07:15.893 --> 00:07:17.353
- I was gonna go to the NBA.

00:07:17.353 --> 00:07:19.021
I knew it was my last game.

00:07:20.606 --> 00:07:21.941
Local kid 

00:07:21.941 --> 00:07:23.317
and a Gonzaga kid for my whole life.

00:07:27.029 --> 00:07:29.240
It was very emotional to,

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:30.658
to lose that way.

00:07:30.658 --> 00:07:32.577
It wasn't like we, you know,

00:07:32.577 --> 00:07:33.536
just got our butts kicked and

00:07:33.536 --> 00:07:35.204
then I just showed emotion like that.

00:07:35.204 --> 00:07:36.164
We were ahead 17.

00:07:39.792 --> 00:07:41.419
- It's kinda how he's wired,

00:07:41.419 --> 00:07:42.753
which is, which is what you respect.

00:07:43.713 --> 00:07:44.839
- If that happened now

00:07:44.839 --> 00:07:45.840
it’d be poignant and,

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:47.049
“Look at this

00:07:47.049 --> 00:07:48.384
man showing emotion.

00:07:48.384 --> 00:07:49.385
How great is this?”

00:07:49.385 --> 00:07:50.678
and all that stuff.

00:07:50.678 --> 00:07:51.304
So,

00:07:51.304 --> 00:07:53.347
you know, it's funny how culture changes

00:07:53.347 --> 00:07:54.599
and everything shifts,

00:07:54.599 --> 00:07:58.102
but I was the first guy to do it, and so I got hammered for it,

00:07:58.102 --> 00:07:59.061
which is OK.

00:07:59.061 --> 00:08:00.062
It happens.

00:08:00.062 --> 00:08:01.898
But if we win that game,

00:08:01.898 --> 00:08:03.816
I'm never remembered for that.

00:08:05.985 --> 00:08:09.030
The previous guy who did the color

00:08:09.197 --> 00:08:10.490
took another job in town,

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:12.033
and so they just called me one day 

00:08:12.033 --> 00:08:13.034
and said, “Do you wanna give it a shot?”

00:08:13.034 --> 00:08:14.410
I've never had any experience.

00:08:14.410 --> 00:08:16.454
There's times when I wish I was wearing a uniform again

00:08:16.454 --> 00:08:18.456
because it’d be fun to play in this offense.

00:08:18.456 --> 00:08:20.082
It helps me stay around the game and

00:08:20.082 --> 00:08:21.459
watch basketball for a living.

00:08:21.459 --> 00:08:22.460
It's good, good life.

00:08:23.586 --> 00:08:27.215
I've had really good life experiences because of basketball,

00:08:27.215 --> 00:08:29.217
and especially that season.

00:08:31.093 --> 00:08:32.386
People have asked me,

00:08:32.386 --> 00:08:34.013
“Whenever you hear UCLA,

00:08:34.013 --> 00:08:34.680
does it freak you out?”

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:35.723
I was like, “No,

00:08:35.765 --> 00:08:36.390
it's all right.

00:08:36.390 --> 00:08:37.308
It's one loss.”

00:08:37.308 --> 00:08:38.226
It happens and

00:08:38.226 --> 00:08:39.227
I'm not, 

00:08:39.310 --> 00:08:41.354
I'm not ashamed of showing emotion

00:08:41.354 --> 00:08:42.355
to be honest.

